messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-tic54x.c
Line: 257
Function: tic54x_lookup_howto
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: When dst->r_symndx == -1, the code adds HOWTO_BANK to the matched index i and sets internal->howto = tic54x_howto_table + i + bank without bounds checking. For relocation type R_RELLONG ("STAB"), the only entry is at index 12 and has no banked counterpart; adding HOWTO_BANK (e.g., 6) yields an index past the end of tic54x_howto_table, leading to an invalid howto pointer that will be dereferenced later. A crafted COFF file with r_symndx == -1 and r_type == R_RELLONG can trigger this.

Source context:
```c
      217:     case BFD_RELOC_TIC54X_MS7_OF_23:
      218:       return &tic54x_howto_table[5];
      219:     case BFD_RELOC_32:
      220:       return &tic54x_howto_table[12];
      221:     default:
      222:       return (reloc_howto_type *) NULL;
      223:     }
      224: }
